            <ArticleTitle>Carotidynia: revisiting an unfamiliar entity.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1144-53</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.avsg.2011.06.006</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Carotidynia (unilateral neck pain reproducible with light pressure on the carotid artery) is a controversial and poorly understood vascular condition. This review provides important historical information, several representative case reports, and a comprehensive summary of the literature. The authors also propose an algorithm for the care of these patients.</AbstractText>
